A||||5||rc5star||Vacuum lines???||||5||
Z||000000||rc5star||07-13-2001||08:07 AM||||When I was taking apart my engine I broke one of the vacuum lines. I was just going to replace the whole harness because they seem real brittle but after all these year wouldnt any replacement be brittle? Should I just try and replace it and take my chances or is their another option??||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||07-13-2001||08:17 AM||||You can buy replacement rubber vacum hose by the foot at any auto supply store new. Just replace all of them you see at same time. if ones bad others will soon follow. Its very cheap stuff. Cut off a small piece to take with you to get the right size.||||reg||1
Z||000002||k2m4||07-13-2001||09:44 AM||||replace them all ...youll get a shitty running car with cracked vacuume lines. pep boys sels 4 feet of lines for 3.50 ...if you want to be cheap about it get some shrink tubing and you can repair the line but ...repair them !<BR>kerm<BR>86 2M4 <BR>86 1/2 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steven||07-13-2001||09:56 AM||||If you don't mind spending more money, you could go to <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  . He sales a vac. line set made from mild steel, and a set made from stainless steel.<BR>**Warning**<BR>You will pay more than $3.50.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jncomutt||07-13-2001||12:12 PM||||Anyone know if anyone makes quality lines like Rodney Dickmans set but for a 4 cyl?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||07-13-2001||07:56 PM||||For the 4 cyl,<P>You can get replacement hard plastic line stock thru many parts stores. IF the rubber ends are still good. The ends can be hard to come by.<P>Unless it's abused the plastic hard line last a long time.<P>To shape it, soak it in hot water to let it warm up. ||||reg||1
